# Runtime install of this project's own skill, plus canary agents and host
# settings. `workforce/` is the source distribution; `.claude/` is a working copy.
/.claude/

# ANCHORED above, and this is load-bearing. As a bare `.claude/` the pattern
# matched at EVERY depth, so it swallowed `fixtures/*/.claude/` — the trees the
# fixtures ARE. Twelve fixtures were committed as a CLAUDE.md and a TRUTH.md
# describing content that was never in the repo, and `bin/conformance` — a gate
# that exits 1 — failed 41 of 60 assertions on a fresh clone while passing here.
# Measured 2026-08-01 by cloning. The corpus is the only instrument that shows
# this system generalizes; ignoring it made a collaborator's checkout unable to
# run the one gate that says so.
!fixtures/*/.claude/

# NOTE: CLAUDE.md is deliberately NOT ignored here, diverging from claude-enforcer.
# Anyone working on this repo needs the orientation, and for a repo-only session —
# remote execution, a collaborator's checkout — the clone is the only copy there is.

# Host-generated snapshots and restore kits. Never committed.
.claude-backups/

# OS and editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# fixture git histories are recreated by fixtures/init-git.sh, never committed
fixtures/*/.git/
